Fillets: a regularity (G1) is put on an edge between a blend and a face
only where the two are tangent along it (mitcad#300).

A rounding whose contact runs along the far edge of a face it consumes (a
boss's foot rounded as high as the boss, the wall vanishing) records its
regularity with the wall (ChFiDS_Regul). The topological build leaves the
contact's edge between the blend and the face beyond (the boss's top), and
SetRegul took that face for the wall's image and marked the edge G1, though
the two meet at a right angle there; likewise for the edges a rounding's
blend makes with the walls of a hole cut through it before. A later
rounding of such an edge then went wrong: on the boss's top edge, one
closed edge, ChFi3d_Builder::PerformElement took the spine as ending at its
vertex (FaceTangency rejects the closed edge's vertex, the faces said to be
tangent), the start was found on the guide's prolongation past the end and
the walk stopped there ("Path failed", for any radius); at a hole's corner
the walk went on past the corner's vertex onto the rounding's torus as if
it continued the hole's wall, and failed. SetRegul now checks the faces'
tangency along the edge (ChFi3d::IsTangentFaces, as for any edge) before it
encodes the regularity.

Upstream: new.
